        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0173" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v11p1/pg124"/>

                <head>49. Memorandum From Director of Central Intelligence Turner<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d49-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1979-11-22">November 22, 1979</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list type="description">
                    <label>MEMORANDUM FOR</label>
                    <item>The President</item>
                    <item>The Vice President</item>
                    <item>The Secretary of State</item>
                    <item>The Secretary of Defense</item>
                    <item>The National Security Advisor</item>
                </list>
                <p>On Tuesday<anchor n="2" xml:id="d49-f2"/> we discussed the pros and cons of the
                    Shah’s departure to some country other than Iran. I have since asked the [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">less than 1 line not declassified</hi>] and Iranian
                    experts to articulate their views on this succinctly. The result is
                    attached.</p>
                <p>I agree with their views, though I am less persuaded that the students in the
                    embassy may act independently of Khomeini. The initial debriefings of our 13
                    released hostages seem to indicate a close loyalty to Khomeini on the part of
                    the student captors.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d49-f3"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold">Stansfield Turner</hi><anchor n="4"
                            xml:id="d49-f4"/></signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d49-a1.xml" xpointer="d49-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
